Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: retire the link on controller transport failure

The connection owns an ordered ACL stream. After the driver rejects a
packet, sending its successors would leave a hole in that stream. Return
the reserved credit and disconnect instead. Drivers that can retry a
definitely unsubmitted packet do so before reporting a terminal failure.

--- a/wireless/bluetooth/bt_conn.c
+++ b/wireless/bluetooth/bt_conn.c
@@ -214,7 +214,10 @@
       if (ret < 0)
         {
           bt_conn_tx_complete(conn, 1);
           wlerr("ACL transport send failed: %d\n", ret);
+          bt_buf_release(buf);
+          (void)bt_conn_disconnect(conn, BT_HCI_ERR_REMOTE_USER_TERM_CONN);
+          break;
         }
 
       bt_buf_release(buf);
